{"event_type":"review","id":"b663fe062b9aeac2de80d70073747d1c685a50186ee4c91a2a3c2f47a98e50c9","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T05:03:38Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0346c0f0afe2c7c2b112ad1d54ecf140fc3652847dd1f9b8e32054b87bd984bf","sha256":"0346c0f0afe2c7c2b112ad1d54ecf140fc3652847dd1f9b8e32054b87bd984bf"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/891e0bc155879c564c07b6cfbe0c4e1281c2d20453bbf4a1bca695553c1ce6a5","sha256":"891e0bc155879c564c07b6cfbe0c4e1281c2d20453bbf4a1bca695553c1ce6a5"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9d8a04d7d98cd7cbea7a48ede93f8603962b9e55ce6e8682c0c1ca9435bda88d","sha256":"9d8a04d7d98cd7cbea7a48ede93f8603962b9e55ce6e8682c0c1ca9435bda88d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/03f72922f4579281162dfc4f1a56c6536411528af92760188f3f3fce176b9192","sha256":"03f72922f4579281162dfc4f1a56c6536411528af92760188f3f3fce176b9192"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/08bde5b6478c188ed892b154f0bed0996d20eb9cbbf93f9e43de12fc69c1fdef","sha256":"08bde5b6478c188ed892b154f0bed0996d20eb9cbbf93f9e43de12fc69c1fdef"}],"attempt_id":"fb1741814315df1ea9ca957b5b534c8cfd5411673679829510ac5f75c713c400:0:1","base":"9ce700b58da7f55ffb022a61f716489ec4e1a580","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"d6e3f6f06dfc9cfae45e296d7a0fa9df137ebb65","body":"**Read the whole `name:` value before treating it as a literal check name.**\n\n`literalOf(lines, nameSpan)` at workflowScan.ts:967 uses the default `wholeValue = false`. It returns only the first line of a `name:` value that wraps onto a more-indented line. Example:\n\n```yaml\n  build:\n    name: ci\n      extra\n```\n\n`classify` (workflowScan.ts:440-443) marks `extra` as a `content` line. GitHub reads the job name as `ci extra`. The scanner sets `name = 'ci'` and `dynamicName = false`. `producersOf(scan, 'ci')` (workflowScan.ts:1037-1045) then returns `build` as a producer of `ci`. That is the phantom producer the module contract says never happens (workflowScan.ts:38-41: \"never 'produces' a check, so the caller sees a missing producer rather than a phantom one\").\n\nImpact: a workflow change can stop producing a required check, and the default-branch policy check still sees a producer. It then raises no needs-human finding. The scanner is meant to over-flag, never under-flag, so `name:` needs the same whole-value reading that `uses:` already gets (workflowScan.ts:975).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    const literal = literalOf(lines, nameSpan);\n+    const literal = literalOf(lines, nameSpan, true);\n```\n</details>\n\nThe `literalOf` doc comment (workflowScan.ts:577-578) says only `uses` opts in. Update it to name `name` too.","id":"5718ecb461323e96b9d1aa37fb81971f24ffbfe8d4861cfb547bf32f399d28bb","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/gates/workflowScan.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Read the whole `name:` value before treating it as a literal check name."}],"head":"5ea451a16030601c53758131c9b09584c1f150f7","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"e2d3ca4919b820bc4d092757036b46ed4edc63c7","intervals":[[1,95]],"path":".github/actions/static-gate/action.yml"},{"blob":"d6e3f6f06dfc9cfae45e296d7a0fa9df137ebb65","intervals":[[1,1462]],"path":"src/ops/gates/workflowScan.ts"}],"job_id":"fb1741814315df1ea9ca957b5b534c8cfd5411673679829510ac5f75c713c400:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"d6e3f6f06dfc9cfae45e296d7a0fa9df137ebb65","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/gates/workflowScan.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},